{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS88SMwZdCwY85oKSRr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the generator. In `gen.py` (`hr_target`), the bottom of the heart-rate range is now sent under the `start` key instead of `value`: `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`. I also added an explanation to the docstring.\n\n**Why:** your watch notes show the API accepted the event, but every range on the watch matched one of the watch's own zones. Changing the watch's threshold heart rate (LTHR) only moved the zone edges. So the problem was the type of target, not the different LTHR values (172 in Intervals vs 168 on the watch). Intervals exports `{value, end}` as a zone target, which the watch snaps to its own zones. It exports `{start, end}` as an Instant-HR range in beats per minute, calculated from Intervals' own LTHR of 172. I kept the targets as percentages of LTHR. Your earlier tries with `bpm` and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` had already shown the units weren't the issue.\n\n**Checked:** `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json` now gives `start`/`end` on all four steps, and `value` no longer appears. I haven't confirmed the fix on the watch, because the rules didn't allow sending anything to Intervals. To check it: push the event, read it back, sync Garmin, and look at the \"Float\" step. It should show 129–141, not 137–151. I left `readback/` as it was, since it records the old version.\n\n**From your colleague's note,** I used three parts:\n- The main fix: `start` instead of `value`, and the explanation of how each one is exported.\n- The step format with percentages, plus the account of the failed `bpm` and `start_bpm` attempts.\n- The read-back-and-watch procedure, written into `ANSWER.md` as a way to check the fix.\n\nI skipped the top-level `description` field and its text format. Your steps already come back filled in, so that problem doesn't apply here. Also, a mistake in `description` can make Intervals erase both copies of the workout's steps. I also skipped the part about the dropdown menu and how to set up API access. All of this is written up in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1794,"cache_read_input_tokens":25262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1794},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87d6a7ef-3901-4528-8f48-bb74ce9b988e","uuid":"c3de8400-31a0-4f16-b3fc-2200d18d46f8","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:38:19.989Z","request_id":"req_011CgS88S64pjsY8oSCuHGij"}
